  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Surveillance for Malaria Elimination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Ethiopia):  Ethiopia has made significant progress in reducing malaria-related morbidity and mortality. Effective surveillance and malaria treatment have been cornerstones of Ethiopia&apos;s successful campaign against malaria. ..The Surveillance for Malaria Elimination (S4ME) Activity supports high quality malaria elimination interventions in 67 low and very low malaria transmission districts and health facilities, as well as efforts to strengthen the capacity of healthcare workers&apos; and district administrators&apos; to understand and use data for effective decision making. ..The Activity tests and develops models of effective malaria elimination by helping to identify and manage all malaria cases occurring in districts. The effort is locally driven and focuses on district-level capacity building, especially malaria surveillance systems in health facilities and communities to improve the ability to detect and report malaria cases. The surveillance systems are designed to detect malaria cases even in hard to reach populations, such as refugees, internally displaced persons, and migrants....</narrative>
  </description>
